      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hastings_Street_(Vancouver)"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The street once hosted Vancouver’s “Great White Way,” a neon‑lit boulevard that drew crowds before becoming the Downtown Eastside.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hastings_Street_(Vancouver)"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early 1900s hotels on East Hastings were built for resource workers and later converted into low‑cost single‑room occupancy housing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://dailyhive.com/vancouver/downtown-eastside-vancouver-photos-before-after"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The former MGM studio on East Hastings was a major film and television production hub in the city.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://dailyhive.com/vancouver/downtown-eastside-vancouver-photos-before-after"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The corner of East Hastings and Cambie houses the historic Carter‑Cotton Building, former headquarters of the Vancouver Province newspaper.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
